00:14:37.430 --> 00:14:39.400
I knew you'd enjoy that one.

00:14:39.400 --> 00:14:43.680
That really, really and truly is a beautiful way to do it.

00:14:43.680 --> 00:14:47.310
Little bit right there.

00:14:47.310 --> 00:14:50.930
And it works so simple, so easy.

00:14:50.930 --> 00:14:54.170
As I say, this is a fantastic first painting to try.

00:14:54.170 --> 00:14:56.680
If you've never painted along with me before,

00:14:56.680 --> 00:14:57.840
this is a good one to try.

00:14:57.840 --> 00:14:59.600
And this is on a black canvas.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:04.130
prepare these black canvases with a flat black acrylic.

00:15:04.130 --> 00:15:05.830
They're painted with a flat black acrylic,

00:15:05.830 --> 00:15:08.260
allowed to dry completely.

00:15:08.260 --> 00:15:10.340
And then we go back and apply the color over them.

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:15.030
And in this case, we applied phthalo blue and sap green.

00:15:15.030 --> 00:15:21.000
Just brush mixed all over the canvas.

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:23.360
And you see what happens.

00:15:23.360 --> 00:15:24.880
Bring some limbs out across the tree

00:15:24.880 --> 00:15:27.320
so they're not all on each side.

00:15:27.320 --> 00:15:29.890
Okay, that'll give you enough practice on

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:32.930
You know how to do them now.

00:15:32.930 --> 00:15:36.310
Okay, let's get up here and play.

00:15:36.310 --> 00:15:39.220
But you can see by pulling those trees down,

00:15:39.220 --> 00:15:42.860
how it creates depth.

00:15:42.860 --> 00:15:48.390
Okay, now we need to cover up his little foots.

00:15:48.390 --> 00:15:50.050
And you can take a little bit of the black color

00:15:50.050 --> 00:15:51.590
on your brush if you want to put a little shadow

00:15:51.590 --> 00:15:53.170
behind these trees.

00:15:53.170 --> 00:15:54.980
See there?

00:15:54.980 --> 00:15:59.350
Easy, easy, you can drop a little shadow right behind them.

00:16:01.180 --> 00:16:02.230
That simple.

00:16:02.230 --> 00:16:05.310
Okay, now we go back into our yellows.

00:16:05.310 --> 00:16:08.900
I got cad yellow, Indian yellow, yellow ochre,

00:16:08.900 --> 00:16:12.600
and here and there a little touch of permanent red.

00:16:12.600 --> 00:16:17.710
Let's just drop in some little soft, quiet, grassy areas.

00:16:17.710 --> 00:16:20.400
A little sap green added to that to dull it down.

00:16:20.400 --> 00:16:24.300
Don't want it to get too bright.

00:16:24.300 --> 00:16:29.040
Isn't that a super way to make a lot of trees fast?

00:16:29.040 --> 00:16:30.000
Let's put some over it.

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:32.730
I can't leave this side out.

00:16:32.730 --> 00:16:34.390
Now all I'm doing is touching the canvas,

00:16:34.390 --> 00:16:38.140
just tapping it, very soft, very quiet.

00:16:38.140 --> 00:16:41.470
Darker, darker, darker as it goes toward the foreground.

00:16:41.470 --> 00:16:46.590
You know, if you had a beautiful place like this,

00:16:46.590 --> 00:16:48.870
I'd want a little house, I'd want to live back here,

00:16:48.870 --> 00:16:50.330
'cause this is where the bunny rabbit lives,

00:16:50.330 --> 00:16:52.270
and you could sit here and you could talk to him,

00:16:52.270 --> 00:16:54.510
and you could have all kind of fun.

00:16:54.510 --> 00:16:56.690
So let's put a little house back here.

00:16:56.690 --> 00:16:59.380
I'm gonna start out with Van Dyke Brown on the knife.

00:17:00.480 --> 00:17:02.200
and just get a little bit of paint.

00:17:02.200 --> 00:17:03.880
Cut across, get that little roll of paint

00:17:03.880 --> 00:17:06.250
right out on the edge of the knife, there you go.

00:17:06.250 --> 00:17:07.400
Okay, let's go up here.

00:17:07.400 --> 00:17:12.790
Maybe our little house lives, shoot, right, right there.

00:17:12.790 --> 00:17:14.270
Right there.

00:17:14.270 --> 00:17:17.870
We'll do the back eave, there we are.

00:17:17.870 --> 00:17:21.830
Let's do the front of the house, zoop, zoop.

00:17:30.320 --> 00:17:33.330
We can straighten out this edge.

00:17:33.330 --> 00:17:35.830
Now there's numerous ways to make houses.

00:17:35.830 --> 00:17:39.350
This is just one, and maybe, maybe in your world,

00:17:39.350 --> 00:17:40.610
there isn't a house back here.

00:17:40.610 --> 00:17:42.550
I just want to show you also how to make a little house

00:17:42.550 --> 00:17:45.100
in the woods if you want one.

00:17:45.100 --> 00:17:48.120
You may not want a house in your painting,

00:17:48.120 --> 00:17:52.600
and this is a beautiful painting without a house.

00:17:52.600 --> 00:17:54.140
So if there's no house in your world,

00:17:54.140 --> 00:17:55.410
don't put one in your painting.

00:18:00.730 --> 00:18:02.330
Maybe he's like me, he ran out of room.

00:18:02.330 --> 00:18:03.430
We'll have to give him a shed.

00:18:03.430 --> 00:18:05.170
I like to make little sheds on the houses,

00:18:05.170 --> 00:18:10.500
little storage areas, or maybe it's where his chicken lives.

00:18:10.500 --> 00:18:12.780
You know, chickens need a house too.

00:18:12.780 --> 00:18:16.810
We'll put a little shed right there and bring it down.

00:18:16.810 --> 00:18:19.520
Okay, okay.

00:18:19.520 --> 00:18:21.460
Now then, let's do some playing.

00:18:21.460 --> 00:18:26.080
I'll take some white, a little bit of Van Dyke Brown,

00:18:26.080 --> 00:18:27.480
a little burnt umber into it.

00:18:27.480 --> 00:18:29.510
White Van Dyke Brown, a little burnt umber.

00:18:31.240 --> 00:18:32.890
There, just mix it up.

00:18:32.890 --> 00:18:34.710
And this we're not going to mix too much.

00:18:34.710 --> 00:18:45.710
We want this to be marbly and we'll just cut across it.

00:18:45.710 --> 00:18:49.400
Barely touch, let it just gently, gently,

00:18:49.400 --> 00:18:50.640
gently slide across there.

00:18:50.640 --> 00:18:53.870
You want that pink to break, make it look old.

00:18:53.870 --> 00:18:55.070
Now I'm gonna take the same color

00:18:55.070 --> 00:18:57.210
and add a little more white to it.

00:18:57.210 --> 00:18:59.320
'Cause we said our light was coming from the left,

00:18:59.320 --> 00:19:00.000
so the front of the camera

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:03.280
cabin would be a little bit brighter than the side.

00:19:03.280 --> 00:19:07.710
Same color with white added to it.

00:19:07.710 --> 00:19:09.730
See, now that stands out better.

00:19:09.730 --> 00:19:13.760
Same color, just a different value.

00:19:13.760 --> 00:19:15.520
Maybe out here there's a, tell you what,

00:19:15.520 --> 00:19:19.380
I'm gonna add a small amount of blue to that

00:19:19.380 --> 00:19:22.810
to cast it into a little shadow.

00:19:22.810 --> 00:19:26.300
Just a little bit right in here.

00:19:26.300 --> 00:19:28.400
Once, a little bit of color on that.

00:19:28.400 --> 00:19:30.000
That's gonna end up being a little

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:31.780
shed.

00:19:31.780 --> 00:19:34.300
Okay, maybe, maybe, tell you what,

00:19:34.300 --> 00:19:36.810
maybe there's some little shingles.

00:19:36.810 --> 00:19:40.410
We'll take some permanent red, a little Van Dyke brown.

00:19:40.410 --> 00:19:42.070
Let's put a few little shingles here,

00:19:42.070 --> 00:19:44.550
or just indications of shingles.

00:19:44.550 --> 00:19:48.810
Da-da-da-da-da, drop 'em in, drop 'em in.

00:19:48.810 --> 00:19:51.010
Just come right across, do it in layers,

00:19:51.010 --> 00:19:55.250
so the top is covered by the bottom of the one above it,

00:19:55.250 --> 00:19:57.240
just like when you put real shingles on.

00:20:01.760 --> 00:20:03.860
That's all there is to it.

00:20:03.860 --> 00:20:06.730
Now we need, let's put a little highlight,

00:20:06.730 --> 00:20:10.200
just so it separates this.

00:20:10.200 --> 00:20:15.610
Just a little bit of highlight.

00:20:15.610 --> 00:20:17.640
Edge.

00:20:17.640 --> 00:20:20.570
Isn't that a cute little cabin out there in the woods?

00:20:20.570 --> 00:20:21.410
I need a door.

00:20:21.410 --> 00:20:23.240
Gotta have a door.

00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:27.040
Can't get in our cabin, the door lives right there.

00:20:27.040 --> 00:20:30.000
And around the door, we need a little bit of light,

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:38.450
so the door stands out, you know.

00:20:38.450 --> 00:20:40.450
Put a little white on there, that'll make it stand out.

00:20:40.450 --> 00:20:44.290
Oh yeah, that's much better against that dark canvas.

00:20:44.290 --> 00:20:48.730
Just a little indication, maybe, maybe, maybe, maybe,

00:20:48.730 --> 00:20:52.490
maybe there's a couple of windows over here.

00:20:52.490 --> 00:20:54.190
There's one, there's one.

00:20:54.190 --> 00:20:58.010
Looks like two big eyes looking at you.

00:20:58.010 --> 00:21:00.000
I want to take a little bit

00:21:00.090 --> 00:21:02.300
and put it there and make it look maybe like

00:21:02.300 --> 00:21:06.100
it's a little light shining across from glass in the window.

00:21:06.100 --> 00:21:08.140
There's a little glass out here.

00:21:08.140 --> 00:21:12.620
A little straightening up.

00:21:12.620 --> 00:21:14.060
Give 'em a little highlight around the window

00:21:14.060 --> 00:21:17.380
so it stands out.

00:21:17.380 --> 00:21:20.160
If you want boards, all you gotta do is cut through this

00:21:20.160 --> 00:21:23.680
and make it look just like little boards.

00:21:23.680 --> 00:21:27.590
They're a cabin, so you do whatever you want.

00:21:27.590 --> 00:21:30.000
Okay, now we need, now we need

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:31.540
we need a little path.

00:21:31.540 --> 00:21:32.540
Let's get up to this cabin.

00:21:32.540 --> 00:21:34.640
So I'll go back into the brown and the burnt umber,

00:21:34.640 --> 00:21:36.390
just sort of mix together.

00:21:36.390 --> 00:21:43.900
And here, there comes a little path.

00:21:43.900 --> 00:21:49.820
And this little path just wanders wherever you want it.

00:21:49.820 --> 00:21:52.090
Let it wander, let it play.

00:21:52.090 --> 00:21:56.180
Van Dyke brown, burnt umber.

00:21:56.180 --> 00:21:58.790
And let it get darker, darker, darker.

00:21:58.790 --> 00:22:00.000
We don't care where it goes.

00:22:01.760 --> 00:22:05.000
Now we can take a little brown and white.

00:22:05.000 --> 00:22:09.120
Barely touch.

00:22:09.120 --> 00:22:10.420
Got a few little indications.

00:22:10.420 --> 00:22:12.560
Looks like there's a little blue in there too.

00:22:12.560 --> 00:22:13.560
A little thalo blue.

00:22:13.560 --> 00:22:15.910
A brown, white, a little thalo blue.

00:22:15.910 --> 00:22:17.500
Barely touch.

00:22:17.500 --> 00:22:20.260
Darker, darker over here.

00:22:20.260 --> 00:22:27.210
Now then, let's go back to our 2 1/2 inch brush.

00:22:27.210 --> 00:22:30.000
A little yellow, sap green.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:35.590
and come back in here.

00:22:35.590 --> 00:22:39.220
And you know, all these beautiful little grassy areas.

00:22:39.220 --> 00:22:42.770
Bring them right down to the edge of this little path,

00:22:42.770 --> 00:22:46.380
little dirt area, just let them go.

00:22:46.380 --> 00:22:53.300
Ochre, cad yellow, Indian yellow, just mix them on the brush.

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:02.980
I'll add a small, small amount of permanent red to that.

00:23:02.980 --> 00:23:06.730
Just, maybe we'll put a little spot right in there.

00:23:06.730 --> 00:23:13.170
Right there, a little too much of that in there.

00:23:13.170 --> 00:23:19.570
Just a little sap green, yellows mainly.

00:23:19.570 --> 00:23:26.040
Just let it go.

00:23:26.040 --> 00:23:27.240
This really is a fun painting.

00:23:27.240 --> 00:23:29.760
I think, I think if you will do this one

00:23:30.380 --> 00:23:31.580
This one will make you happy.

00:23:31.580 --> 00:23:36.950
It'll make your heart feel good, make you happy.

00:23:36.950 --> 00:23:38.970
And that's what painting's all about.

00:23:38.970 --> 00:23:42.510
Painting should make you happy.

00:23:42.510 --> 00:23:45.550
Should make you happy.

00:23:45.550 --> 00:23:47.670
Okay, let's go to the other side.

00:23:47.670 --> 00:23:49.130
A little bit right, look at that.

00:23:49.130 --> 00:23:49.970
See how easy it is?

00:23:49.970 --> 00:23:52.520
All I'm doing is touching the canvas and sort of,

00:23:52.520 --> 00:23:53.820
just barely bending down.

00:23:53.820 --> 00:23:54.900
Don't let the brush slide, though.

00:23:54.900 --> 00:23:56.880
Just tap it, don't let it slide on it.

00:23:56.880 --> 00:24:00.000
If it slides, it'll just make streaks and you

00:24:00.120 --> 00:24:02.040
Pretty soon you end up mixing mud.

00:24:02.040 --> 00:24:05.130
We don't want to be mud mixers.

00:24:05.130 --> 00:24:07.720
Very soft, quiet.

00:24:07.720 --> 00:24:10.400
And if you get one that's too bright or too distinct,

00:24:10.400 --> 00:24:12.900
all you have to do is tap it a few times.

00:24:12.900 --> 00:24:16.300
It'll pick up the color it's underneath and it'll go away.

00:24:16.300 --> 00:24:19.020
It'll just go to whatever you want it to be.

00:24:19.020 --> 00:24:21.640
Very, very soft, very quiet.

00:24:21.640 --> 00:24:24.090
Maybe, tell you what, I'll go into a little bit of sap,

00:24:24.090 --> 00:24:25.910
green and yellow with a one inch brush.

00:24:25.910 --> 00:24:27.680
I'll do that.

00:24:27.680 --> 00:24:30.000
I want to keep this quite dark, quite dark.

00:24:31.280 --> 00:24:32.830
Okay, let's go up here.

00:24:32.830 --> 00:24:36.350
Maybe there's a little bush here and there

00:24:36.350 --> 00:24:38.650
that just grows around the edge of the house.

00:24:38.650 --> 00:24:41.730
There he is, there he is, wherever you want him.

00:24:41.730 --> 00:24:43.890
See, you can add these little bushes and stuff in here.

00:24:43.890 --> 00:24:46.780
Maybe this guy didn't cut his yard too well,

00:24:46.780 --> 00:24:48.060
and it's beginning to grow.

00:24:48.060 --> 00:24:50.700
Now let's go right, put a little one right there.

00:24:50.700 --> 00:24:51.860
Little light's hitting this one.

00:24:51.860 --> 00:24:53.200
I want it a little brighter.

00:24:53.200 --> 00:24:57.680
Yeah, comes right down in front of that big tree.

00:25:02.270 --> 00:25:04.070
Sap green.

00:25:04.070 --> 00:25:05.820
We'll put one way back in here.

00:25:05.820 --> 00:25:07.330
I don't want this one to be very bright.

00:25:07.330 --> 00:25:09.690
I don't want it to be far away.

00:25:09.690 --> 00:25:13.580
We can drop a few of 'em.

00:25:13.580 --> 00:25:14.910
Let 'em come right over the land area.

00:25:14.910 --> 00:25:17.320
That pushes the land down into the painting.

00:25:17.320 --> 00:25:19.160
Sometimes when you do land or paths,

00:25:19.160 --> 00:25:20.660
or little roads or something,

00:25:20.660 --> 00:25:24.400
you have the feeling that it's floating above the painting.

00:25:24.400 --> 00:25:28.590
If that happens, bring some of this and bring it over it.

00:25:28.590 --> 00:25:30.000
Let it come literally over

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:32.360
part of it, and it'll push the path or the land

00:25:32.360 --> 00:25:34.300
right down into the painting.

00:25:34.300 --> 00:25:35.860
It makes it fit so much better,

00:25:35.860 --> 00:25:38.700
and you'll be happier with it.

00:25:38.700 --> 00:25:41.180
Okay, I think we've about got that.

00:25:41.180 --> 00:25:46.610
Might take and put the tiniest little bit of highlight

00:25:46.610 --> 00:25:49.180
right up here on the top of this roof,

00:25:49.180 --> 00:25:52.660
just to make that little shed stand out a little better.

00:25:52.660 --> 00:25:56.520
And I think it just about gives us a finished painting.

00:25:56.520 --> 00:25:59.410
I'm gonna sign this one, use a little bit of thin oil,

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:02.450
And when I use a thin oil, I usually use something

00:26:02.450 --> 00:26:06.940
like linseed oil or copal, whatever.

00:26:06.940 --> 00:26:08.330
Whatever, just thin oil.

00:26:08.330 --> 00:26:10.170
And we can sign this one.

00:26:10.170 --> 00:26:11.730
I hope you've enjoyed it.

00:26:11.730 --> 00:26:13.540
It's taught you a lot.

00:26:13.540 --> 00:26:14.800
I really do hope you try this one

00:26:14.800 --> 00:26:17.760
because you'll find it to be a great deal of fun.

00:26:17.760 --> 00:26:19.150
And from all of us here,

00:26:19.150 --> 00:26:21.070
I'd like to wish you happy painting.

00:26:21.070 --> 00:26:21.760
God bless.
